WEBVTT

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:31.900
Usain Bolt starts to catch him.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.521
Usain Bolt passes him, and as
the runners come to the finish,

00:01:33.521 --> 00:01:36.198
you'll hear a beep as each man crosses the line.

00:01:36.198 --> 00:01:37.875
(Beeps)

00:01:37.875 --> 00:01:40.980
That's the entire finish of the race.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.360
You can open your eyes now.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.970
That first beep was Usain Bolt.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.284
That last beep was Jesse Owens.

00:01:47.284 --> 00:01:49.461
Listen to it again.

00:01:49.461 --> 00:01:51.179
(Beeps)

00:01:51.179 --> 00:01:52.279
When you think of it like that,

00:01:52.279 --> 00:01:54.550
it's not that big a difference, is it?

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:56.407
And then consider that Usain Bolt started

00:01:56.407 --> 00:01:59.170
by propelling himself out of blocks

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:01.509
down a specially fabricated carpet